WEBVTT

00:00:01.386 --> 00:00:05.008
It seems today that all you see

00:00:05.032 --> 00:00:08.233
Is violence in
movies and sex on TV

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:11.886
But where are those
Good old-fashioned values

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.475
On which we used to rely?

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:18.268
Lucky there's a family guy

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.521
Lucky there's a man who
Positively can do

00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:23.106
All the things that make us

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.941
Laugh and cry

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:30.071
He's a family guy

00:00:35.872 --> 00:00:37.962
Oh, hi, you guys. How was school?

00:00:38.046 --> 00:00:39.214
Eh, it was fine.

00:00:39.297 --> 00:00:42.759
But we had a substitute bully today
and he was doing it wrong.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.652
Okay, it says "tape sign on back."

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.721
Is that... Is that your back, my back?

00:00:46.805 --> 00:00:49.300
I-I got to be honest,
I only got called in 45 minutes ago.

00:00:49.808 --> 00:00:52.519
Just pinch my nipples
and get out of here.

00:00:52.602 --> 00:00:54.771
We need you to
sign these permission slips.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.162
We're taking a school field trip
to Washington DC.

00:00:57.283 --> 00:01:00.161
Great, bring 'em here
and I'll give you my John Hancock.

00:01:00.186 --> 00:01:03.029
-Who's that?
-I'm sorry, I mean my Lane Bryant.

00:01:03.113 --> 00:01:04.989
Well, just say that, then.

00:01:09.398 --> 00:01:13.610
Big day, gentlemen. It's the one day
a year Peter eats a salad.

00:01:13.949 --> 00:01:17.252
Poor bastard. No one should have to
go through that hell.

00:01:17.511 --> 00:01:20.806
He made a promise to Lois.
It was actually in their wedding vows.

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:23.433
All right, let's get this over with.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.686
I brought the whitest-looking lettuce
from McDonald's I could find.

00:01:26.769 --> 00:01:29.314
I'm hoping it has McNugget
smell accidentally on it.

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:32.915
I brought today's newspaper like you asked
so you'd have proof of salad.

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:34.348
Got it.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.244
I love my wife. I love my wife.

00:01:43.328 --> 00:01:44.954
I love my wife.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.927
And inside this local tavern,

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:02.472
a portly gentleman has just consumed
his annual salad.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.932
I'm Garrison Keillor,

00:02:04.015 --> 00:02:09.270
and I was "MeToo'd" for quaintly groping,
so now I'm doing this.

00:02:13.735 --> 00:02:17.339
So, Chris, Meg, you guys excited
for your big trip to Washington DC?

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.281
Yeah. The cool kids are
bringing a candy-colored version

00:02:20.365 --> 00:02:23.451
of whatever drug the media is
most freaking parents out about.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.161
-What?
-Relax, Mom.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.705
We're being supervised
by public school employees

00:02:27.789 --> 00:02:30.917
who themselves are battling
their own crippling addictions.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.418
Peter, are you hearing this?

00:02:32.502 --> 00:02:35.421
I'm not. I'm chewing Cap'n Crunch,
I can't hear anything.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:40.510
I just worry,
but I guess that's what moms do.

00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:44.389
Well, that and give you a recap of
everyone who's died that you don't know.

00:02:44.472 --> 00:02:46.391
You know, Leonard died.

00:02:46.474 --> 00:02:47.976
-Who?
-Leonard.

00:02:48.059 --> 00:02:50.395
-Okay.
-Estelle's pretty upset.

00:02:50.478 --> 00:02:52.605
And right on the heels of Abner.

00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:55.132
You should probably call Edith.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.110
I'll give you Alfred's number.

00:02:57.193 --> 00:02:58.903
Who the hell are these people?

00:02:58.987 --> 00:03:01.864
Is this just an excuse
to say old people's names?

00:03:03.619 --> 00:03:04.490
Vivian.

00:03:31.894 --> 00:03:33.563
What's the matter?
You look upset.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:37.567
Eh, it's just, Joe's been pretty stingy
with his "ha ha's" over text.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.777
I think you're probably
reading into that.

00:03:39.861 --> 00:03:43.400
No, seriously. Cleveland sends some
lame crap and Joe "ha ha's" it.

00:03:43.425 --> 00:03:47.096
I send a photo of me hanging a foreclosure
notice over a toilet, nothing.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.652
I'm telling you, he never laughs
at anything of mine.

00:03:49.745 --> 00:03:51.447
He must have given you
one at some point.

00:03:51.604 --> 00:03:53.495
I mean, sure, at some point.

00:04:25.845 --> 00:04:28.570
Oh, my God.
He's literally never given me one.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.495
Joe doesn't think I'm funny?

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:33.639
Oh, thank God you're here.
You know funny when you hear it.

00:04:34.036 --> 00:04:37.075
Hey, Ostrich, did you hear that crazy
story about the monkey's favorite food?

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:39.077
It's bananas.

00:04:44.109 --> 00:04:47.290
Hey, gang, I know you're not used to
seeing your teachers in shorts,

00:04:47.315 --> 00:04:49.942
so let's get it all out of the way.

00:04:51.396 --> 00:04:54.315
They're just legs, guys.
Oh, one more thing.

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:57.213
We do have a surprise chaperone
for this trip.

00:04:57.395 --> 00:05:01.023
Everyone say hi to
Chris and Meg's mom, Lois Griffin.

00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:03.303
Aah! Woot, woot!

00:05:03.328 --> 00:05:06.206
Did somebody say "cool mom
with an Activia fanny pack"?

00:05:06.231 --> 00:05:08.689
They give you a free one
if you send in enough lids.

00:05:08.714 --> 00:05:11.519
I've got two fanny packs
and a very healthy colon.

00:05:12.061 --> 00:05:14.355
Our chaperone is Mom?

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:18.359
You're lucky. My mother died last year
after a long illness.

00:05:18.443 --> 00:05:22.530
You got your GoFundMe money,
so shut up!

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:31.748
Mom, what the hell
are you doing here?

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.833
Are you trying
to kill our reputation?

00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:37.754
Oh, relax, you two.
I'm gonna be the cool mom, huh?

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.506
I may even have the kids
call me Mrs. G.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.467
Mrs. G.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.760
Can you imagine?

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.179
Just like Mrs. Garrett
from The Facts of Life.

00:05:46.204 --> 00:05:48.039
Nobody knows who that is.

00:05:48.239 --> 00:05:50.950
Come on. Tootie? Blair? Jo?

00:05:50.975 --> 00:05:52.518
Bitch, what you talking about?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.955
Just settle down, you guys.
I promise I won't embarrass you.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.275
Okay, everyone, I've got candy.

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.986
Everybody reach in
but just take one.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:05.406
Fanny candy?
Fanny candy? Fanny candy?

00:06:05.606 --> 00:06:07.733
Oh, my God, this is terrible.

00:06:07.758 --> 00:06:11.554
This is more embarrassing
than when I tried to return that RealDoll.

00:06:11.752 --> 00:06:15.917
Uh, yes, hello, I would
like to return my RealDoll.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.941
Okay,
and what condition is the doll in?

00:06:18.966 --> 00:06:21.844
Um, let's say "fair."

00:06:22.103 --> 00:06:24.735
-Any visible marks?
-Some light choking.

00:06:24.813 --> 00:06:27.196
We can't take the doll back
if there are choke marks.

00:06:27.221 --> 00:06:29.722
Oh, no, no, no,
the choke marks are on me,

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:32.517
and in her defense,
I did have it coming.

00:06:32.638 --> 00:06:34.890
Actually, I don't
want to return the RealDoll.

00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:36.604
This is just part of the dance.

00:06:36.687 --> 00:06:40.441
Oh, no. I didn't realize
you were there the whole time.

00:06:40.525 --> 00:06:43.653
I hope I'm not in for some light choking.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:49.617
Why do you even care if Joe's never
laughed at your texts?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:53.371
Brian, I know it seems like
I have it all, but even I,

00:06:53.454 --> 00:06:57.959
a man with 15 Halloween masks,
have my struggles with insecurity.

00:06:58.042 --> 00:06:59.502
So, what are you gonna do?

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:02.088
I decided to give him
a taste of his own medicine.

00:07:02.113 --> 00:07:06.159
From this day forward, I will never laugh
at another one of Joe's texts.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:16.269
His-his mind just works
in a different way than mine.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.579
Oh, no. Accidental heart,
accidental heart.

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.273
Quick, replace it with a "ha ha."

00:07:20.356 --> 00:07:23.234
Phew, that was close.
I was almost gay.

00:07:23.317 --> 00:07:26.362
Peter just came out of the closet.

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:27.488
Uh, no he didn't.

00:07:27.572 --> 00:07:30.658
The heart emoji:
careful, straight dudes!

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:36.289
Look at us.

00:07:36.372 --> 00:07:39.292
Different generations
enjoying a fancy resort.

00:07:40.001 --> 00:07:42.628
-Mom, don't, please.
-Quiet, Meg.

00:07:42.712 --> 00:07:46.132
So, I saw a really funny TikTok.
Do you know that one?

00:07:46.215 --> 00:07:49.302
You're gonna have to be
more specific. Which one?

00:07:49.385 --> 00:07:51.052
Uh, there's-there's more than one?

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:53.306
Why is everyone leaving?

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:55.513
You're lame
and we don't want to be with you.

00:07:55.549 --> 00:07:58.260
Come on, guys,
let's go watch CNBC in the lobby.

00:07:58.519 --> 00:08:00.813
Yeah, I think I saw a bowl of bananas.

00:08:11.073 --> 00:08:12.783
God, those kids are a nightmare.

00:08:12.808 --> 00:08:14.893
They're just so mean.

00:08:15.036 --> 00:08:17.538
Just be thankful
this isn't your entire life.

00:08:17.622 --> 00:08:20.166
You get to go home
at the end of all of this

00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:22.251
to a family
and someone you love.

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:25.680
Oh, come on, I'm sure there's
someone special in your life.

00:08:26.356 --> 00:08:28.900
You know, there was someone.

00:08:28.925 --> 00:08:30.301
A long time ago.

00:08:32.303 --> 00:08:35.932
It was 1993,
and I was folding clothes at a Structure.

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:37.433
Everyone was, back then.

00:08:37.594 --> 00:08:39.429
Then I saw her.

00:08:40.102 --> 00:08:41.812
Shelly Barnes.

00:08:41.938 --> 00:08:43.564
Boy, was she something.

00:08:43.843 --> 00:08:47.417
Tall, tan. She was more scrunchie
than woman.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.032
We wanted the dream:

00:08:53.115 --> 00:08:55.785
our own Taco Bell franchise.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.037
But then it happened,

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.248
the one thing
you never want to hear.

00:09:00.331 --> 00:09:02.375
Hey, John.
I was just thinking.

00:09:02.458 --> 00:09:05.878
What if we open a Taco Bell/Pizza Hut?

00:09:11.009 --> 00:09:15.179
The psychic who told me to do this
never said anything about Pizza Hut.

00:09:16.138 --> 00:09:17.765
I was young and bullheaded.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:21.169
I had these ideas
of what fast food should be.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.729
Worst part was,
when I told her the bad news,

00:09:23.813 --> 00:09:25.395
she threw my retainer
right in the bushes.

00:09:25.688 --> 00:09:28.416
I looked for a little bit, but eventually
I just said, "Eh, screw it."

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.530
Anyway, that one argument
consumed us.

00:09:32.613 --> 00:09:34.657
Never saw Shelly again.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.451
I'm so sorry to hear all that,
Principal Shepherd.

00:09:37.535 --> 00:09:40.371
Whew, what a day.

00:09:40.454 --> 00:09:42.707
-I need a drink.
-Jack on the rocks?

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.419
No, in the toilet,
but I'll have that drink now.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:53.259
Hey, Joe, you know, you might want to
contact your cell carrier.

00:09:53.342 --> 00:09:56.304
All your "ha ha's" are coming through
as "thumbs up" lately.

00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:57.788
-Oh, boy.
-What's, uh...

00:09:57.822 --> 00:10:00.366
What's with you never laughing
at any of my texts?

00:10:00.391 --> 00:10:02.059
Peter, maybe now's not the time.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:04.912
-No, no, no, tell me. What is it?
-Honestly? Nothing.

00:10:04.996 --> 00:10:07.415
I just don't always think
you're all that funny.

00:10:09.916 --> 00:10:10.450
Wow.

00:10:11.169 --> 00:10:13.379
Uh, okay. Wow.

00:10:13.463 --> 00:10:16.048
Look, if I want someone
to burp the national anthem,

00:10:16.332 --> 00:10:18.626
there is no second call,
it's you or nobody.

00:10:18.887 --> 00:10:21.212
Thank you, Joe.
Thank you for saying that.

00:10:21.295 --> 00:10:24.006
When it comes to laughs,
you're just not my cup of tea.

00:10:24.031 --> 00:10:25.907
I've never even seen Austin Powers.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.468
Oh, well, there you go!

00:10:27.551 --> 00:10:31.263
All right, fellas, I got to run.
Look, this doesn't change anything, Peter.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.791
You're my friend.
No hard feelings.

00:10:33.891 --> 00:10:36.394
Oh yeah, no hard feelings,
like your dink?

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:39.021
I'll see you around, Peter.

00:10:39.993 --> 00:10:41.928
I'll tell you what,
I'm gonna get a laugh from him.

00:10:42.967 --> 00:10:44.485
I'm not sure about that.

00:10:44.568 --> 00:10:46.445
Seems like
he's prayed on this one.

00:10:46.529 --> 00:10:48.739
Well, I'm gonna
give it the old college try.

00:10:49.725 --> 00:10:51.852
-Are you gonna go to class?
-No.

00:10:55.985 --> 00:10:58.279
There you are.
You're not gonna believe this.

00:10:58.304 --> 00:11:00.257
They got the blood
out of the ice machine?

00:11:00.302 --> 00:11:03.305
-No, I found your ex on Facebook.
-What?

00:11:03.521 --> 00:11:07.066
Shelly Barnes. She lives only,
like, 30 miles from here.

00:11:07.149 --> 00:11:09.568
Hmm. Is 30 miles enough time

00:11:09.593 --> 00:11:11.565
for me to get totally jacked
before I see her?

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:14.510
You can do push-ups
in the bus aisle. Let's go find her.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.982
Hey, listen up.

00:11:19.007 --> 00:11:20.921
Anyone seen Principal Shepherd?

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:23.865
He said he had to go to the men's room
and he disappeared.

00:11:23.875 --> 00:11:25.126
I'm not sure.

00:11:25.209 --> 00:11:28.110
I think we're all finger-blasting
anything that moves back here.

00:11:28.872 --> 00:11:29.818
I'll be right back.

00:11:30.801 --> 00:11:34.055
Excuse me, have you seen
a heavyset, middle-aged man?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.582
Kind of sad-looking?

00:11:42.287 --> 00:11:45.954
Hey, you know, there was a guy that
left in a yellow cab a few minutes ago.

00:11:45.979 --> 00:11:48.307
He got the number from
a magazine in his pocket.

00:11:48.391 --> 00:11:51.352
I've never seen such
stretched-out pockets on a sport coat.

00:11:51.587 --> 00:11:52.979
Oh, my God, that's him.

00:11:53.062 --> 00:11:55.106
Principal Shepherd
must have run away.

00:11:55.443 --> 00:11:57.563
Do you have any security footage
from the lobby?

00:11:57.588 --> 00:12:00.591
Sorry, the only video we have
is from the karaoke lounge.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.655
He killed "Sublime", by the way.

00:12:02.781 --> 00:12:05.618
I don't practice Santeria

00:12:05.658 --> 00:12:08.244
I ain't got no crystal ball

00:12:08.327 --> 00:12:11.080
Well, I had a million dollars but...

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:13.291
Don't take those fries.
I'm not done.

00:12:13.433 --> 00:12:15.685
I'd spend it all
If I could find...

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.797
I-I... Ugh, I lost my place.
Start it over from the top, Gene.

00:12:25.401 --> 00:12:27.827
Okay, guys,
Principal Shepherd is gone.

00:12:27.863 --> 00:12:29.573
Did you check
the karaoke lounge?

00:12:29.657 --> 00:12:31.784
He got in a huge fight
with that Gene guy.

00:12:31.925 --> 00:12:33.719
I know you think adults are lame.

00:12:33.744 --> 00:12:36.288
That we're just big bags of crap
that drink coffee,

00:12:36.372 --> 00:12:37.606
but we are people, too.

00:12:37.631 --> 00:12:40.935
Most of the things you think
are important now aren't.

00:12:41.221 --> 00:12:45.131
Looks fade, waists expand,
chins double and dreams die.

00:12:45.214 --> 00:12:47.174
And one day, one day, you're gonna wish

00:12:47.258 --> 00:12:49.468
that a bus full of punk kids
would come along

00:12:49.552 --> 00:12:51.178
and help when you need it most.

00:12:51.476 --> 00:12:54.619
Now, that man is scared and alone,
and he needs us right now.

00:12:54.682 --> 00:12:55.891
Now, who's with me?

00:13:01.467 --> 00:13:03.807
Wait a minute,
if Principal Shepherd's gone,

00:13:03.891 --> 00:13:05.434
who's gonna drive the bus?

00:13:08.989 --> 00:13:11.874
Someone say something
about a bus driver?

00:13:12.124 --> 00:13:14.502
I still need six hours
of supervised road time

00:13:14.585 --> 00:13:15.920
for my B Class license,

00:13:16.003 --> 00:13:18.422
but I'm pretty sure
I can handle this bad boy...

00:13:18.506 --> 00:13:21.258
Meg, let's go find our principal.

00:13:29.433 --> 00:13:30.935
Ooh, sorry.

00:13:31.018 --> 00:13:34.522
Sorry, guys. I got some, but I think
the troublemaker's still in there.

00:13:37.733 --> 00:13:41.695
Can someone please turn
on the always-1978 bus radio?

00:13:43.405 --> 00:13:46.325
I cried a tear...

00:13:47.743 --> 00:13:51.038
You wiped it dry...

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.251
It's not my fault. It's a ballad.

00:13:57.878 --> 00:14:00.089
songs you can't poop over on a bus.

00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:02.925
Soft stoolin' our way through the '70s.

00:14:03.008 --> 00:14:05.427
I love you...

00:14:07.471 --> 00:14:10.349
I honestly love you...

00:14:12.476 --> 00:14:14.812
Change the damn station!

00:14:19.018 --> 00:14:20.139
Whoa, whoa.
Where you going?

00:14:20.359 --> 00:14:22.984
I've had it, Brian.
I am getting a "ha ha" from Joe

00:14:23.009 --> 00:14:24.594
if it's the last thing I do.

00:14:24.638 --> 00:14:26.095
And how are you planning
to do this?

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:29.700
I'm gonna send a funny text
and sneak over to Joe's and "ha ha" it.

00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.704
But why are you wearing all black?

00:14:31.787 --> 00:14:35.291
So no one will see me.

00:14:37.293 --> 00:14:39.879
- Aah!
- Why are you wearing all black?

00:14:39.962 --> 00:14:41.953
Why are you wearing
a lady's ball gown?

00:14:42.699 --> 00:14:45.019
Let's both resume
whatever it is we were doing.

00:15:28.941 --> 00:15:30.109
Who's there?

00:15:33.449 --> 00:15:35.659
Don't struggle.
It only makes it tighter.

00:15:48.422 --> 00:15:50.924
Peter? What the hell
is going on here?

00:15:51.008 --> 00:15:53.093
Joe? Joe, are you okay?

00:15:53.177 --> 00:15:55.012
Yeah, I'm fine, Bon.

00:16:00.315 --> 00:16:03.944
We looked all night and there's no sign
of Principal Shepherd anywhere.

00:16:04.715 --> 00:16:07.510
Oh, my God, of course.
Stop the bus, Meg. Look!

00:16:09.943 --> 00:16:11.028
Gotcha.

00:16:16.033 --> 00:16:19.703
-I thought I might find you here.
-Mrs. Griffin, I, uh...

00:16:19.787 --> 00:16:21.622
Look, I wanted to say I'm sorry.

00:16:21.705 --> 00:16:24.875
I... I shouldn't have inserted
myself into your personal life.

00:16:24.958 --> 00:16:26.585
That... That was wrong of me.

00:16:26.668 --> 00:16:28.670
I know you just wanted to help.
I just...

00:16:29.061 --> 00:16:32.066
I just panicked.
I got so scared of her seeing me now

00:16:32.091 --> 00:16:34.009
and thinking that
I'm this big loser.

00:16:34.093 --> 00:16:36.512
Hey, you are not a loser.

00:16:36.537 --> 00:16:40.833
May I remind you I wear
Saucony sneakers and Lee jeans.

00:16:41.814 --> 00:16:42.556
You...

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:44.804
You are not a loser.

00:16:56.281 --> 00:16:59.535
Mrs. Griffin,
yo quiero one more chance.

00:17:02.621 --> 00:17:05.332
Well, Mr. Griffin, the surgery
went according to plan.

00:17:05.415 --> 00:17:07.000
Great, thank you, Dr. Hartman.

00:17:07.084 --> 00:17:09.378
I didn't know how to
categorize your injuries

00:17:09.403 --> 00:17:11.725
on the insurance form,
so I just put "gay stabbing."

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.040
Oh, okay, who else...
who else sees that?

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:16.552
Oh, almost-almost nobody.

00:17:16.635 --> 00:17:19.054
It's just for, like,
file-keeping record stuff.

00:18:03.982 --> 00:18:04.850
Go get 'em.

00:18:11.992 --> 00:18:12.983
Shelly?

00:18:13.066 --> 00:18:15.819
Hi, it's, uh, it's me, John Shepherd.

00:18:15.903 --> 00:18:17.988
-Listen, John, I-I think maybe--
-Hang on.

00:18:18.113 --> 00:18:19.627
Just-just let me say what I want to say.

00:18:20.056 --> 00:18:21.575
God, you look great.

00:18:21.658 --> 00:18:24.453
Listen, I know it must be odd
to see me standing here

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.269
all these years later.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.749
And although I look like a man
on the outside--

00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:30.693
Shelly lives in the house next door.

00:18:30.834 --> 00:18:32.920
Oh. Oh, uh, uh, which, uh...

00:18:33.178 --> 00:18:35.097
Oh, the one with the aboveground pool

00:18:35.122 --> 00:18:37.624
and angry dogs tied
to the tree in the front yard.

00:18:43.889 --> 00:18:45.974
No way. John Shepherd?

00:18:46.099 --> 00:18:47.684
Is that really you?

00:18:47.809 --> 00:18:49.937
It is. Shelly?

00:18:51.346 --> 00:18:54.066
Shut up! Shut up, you idiots!

00:18:54.149 --> 00:18:56.610
I'd invite you in,
but my uncle's getting dialysis

00:18:56.635 --> 00:18:58.929
-right here in the bonus room.
-Oh, wow.

00:18:59.054 --> 00:19:01.807
Uh, listen, I was...
I was just in the neighborhood.

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:04.143
I wanted to come by
and see how you've been.

00:19:04.226 --> 00:19:06.270
Yeah, not too bad.

00:19:06.353 --> 00:19:09.231
You know, I ended up opening
the Taco Bell/Pizza Hut,

00:19:09.314 --> 00:19:11.066
but it never really took off.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:13.527
I think, ultimately,
it came down to me trading

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:15.904
too many pizzas for drugs.

00:19:15.988 --> 00:19:17.489
Right, right.

00:19:17.514 --> 00:19:20.017
Listen, I actually got
to get these kids somewhere.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:22.427
Well, it was nice
to see you, John.

00:19:22.452 --> 00:19:24.667
You ever want to hang out,
you know where to find me.

00:19:26.269 --> 00:19:29.334
You'll find her in the wind
and in the trees around you.

00:19:29.418 --> 00:19:31.920
Where the leaves blow
and the river flows.

00:19:32.004 --> 00:19:33.589
I'm sorry, who are you?

00:19:33.614 --> 00:19:36.742
I'm Jared Fogle,
the former Subway spokesperson.

00:19:36.925 --> 00:19:39.178
Not sure I want you
in my thought bubble.

00:19:39.261 --> 00:19:40.804
-Aren't you in prison?
-Yes.

00:19:40.929 --> 00:19:43.098
This is how I spend my days
in my cell.

00:19:43.551 --> 00:19:45.851
Hey, how many kids
you got on this bus, by the way?

00:19:45.934 --> 00:19:49.438
This is why!
This is why I don't want you in there!

00:19:54.568 --> 00:19:57.487
Thanks for pushing me
to go find my first love.

00:19:57.571 --> 00:19:59.781
Sorry it ended up being
such a waste of time.

00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:01.617
No, this was not a waste.

00:20:01.742 --> 00:20:03.410
You just found out you won.

00:20:03.535 --> 00:20:04.870
I did? How so?

00:20:04.953 --> 00:20:07.352
Your ex-girlfriend
is a total loser.

00:20:07.508 --> 00:20:09.808
Meanwhile, you have
a great job with a pension,

00:20:09.833 --> 00:20:13.212
a house and a car
with all different-color doors.

00:20:14.598 --> 00:20:15.552
You're right.

00:20:15.577 --> 00:20:17.871
I guess old Shep's doing okay.

00:20:18.191 --> 00:20:20.360
You sure are.
Now, all you got to do

00:20:20.385 --> 00:20:23.222
is just not humiliate yourself
on a bus full of children.

00:20:23.447 --> 00:20:24.781
Ooh, on that note,

00:20:24.806 --> 00:20:27.684
I got to make a quick stop
in the little boy's room.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:31.571
Turn on the radio!

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.858
You're looking kind of lonely, girl...

00:20:36.568 --> 00:20:38.278
Would you like someone new...

00:20:39.613 --> 00:20:42.115
This bowl's getting very full.

00:20:42.199 --> 00:20:45.160
I strongly suggest
we don't go up or down any hills.

00:20:45.244 --> 00:20:47.412
I'm feeling kind of lonely, too

00:20:47.537 --> 00:20:49.039
If you don't mind

00:20:49.122 --> 00:20:51.708
Can I sit down here beside you?

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:57.464
All right.